Z||000011||stimpy||07-11-2001||12:37 AM||||I have Bridgestone Turanza H Revos on my car in stock GT sizes. They are kinda pricy, but definately a high tech tire. Very quiet tires with good wet control. They have a dual compound, so as the tire wears, a soft compound comes through. The harder compound surrounds the soft compound, so you get the stickiness without the fast wear. ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Areakon||07-11-2001||01:22 AM||||I can get the BFG Radial T/A for about $38. I would stay away from them though. Here lately we have had a lot of them coming back in out of round. And BFG doesn't want to accept them back. I also have a set on one of my cars and they are also on the wobbly side.<p>[This message has been edited by Areakon (edited 07-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Oreif||07-11-2001||02:35 AM||||I have always used BFGoodrich tires since the late 70's and I have never had a problem with any types. (T/A, Comp T/A, T/A-R's, All-Terrain T/A's, and Euro T/A's) My present Fiero has Euro T/A's and they work GREAT!||||reg||1
Z||000014||Jncomutt||07-11-2001||03:27 AM||||Its BFGoodrich I believe that makes the tires called "Scorcher"  They have like 3 verticle stripes in the tread that come in a variety of colors, Yellow being one of them.  I'm really too sure how they are for size however||||reg||1
Z||000015||Hartz||07-11-2001||08:21 AM||||OK, I know you're looking for 14 inch tires, but for anyone who might be thinking of 16's and looking for a good deal, I just got 4 P225/50/16 Firestone SZ50s (same tire as on Pontiac Firehawk) for $73 each from the Tire Rack.<P>I have these tires (bigger size) on my Firehawk, and my buddy has them on his Cobra, and we both have been very pleased with them.  I am looking forward to trying them on the Fiero.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Hartz<P>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo||||reg||6
Z||000016||Leadfoot||07-11-2001||11:43 AM||||Thanks guys!  I just had to by a pair of yoko's sp(something) since the back left blew out yesterday.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  The rear tires had 2 huge cracks along the circumference so I wasn't totally surprized this happened.  On the plus side I put on the polished wheels and they look sweet.  The tire guys dismounted the other 2 tires from the rear wheels so I should have them polished by friday.  Once I have all four polished I will buy the T/A tires.  I'll probable have the yoko's put one my extra set of rims (which I might polish as well) and keep them for a rainy day or sell them. ||||reg||1
Z||000017||DreXteR||07-11-2001||09:04 PM||||I believe you should get a good set of Z rated tires, those are AA traction. I bougth a set of ultraZ from pepboy for my Grand Vitara 245/50/16 couldnt afford any name brand, BUT... DAMN those tires are AWESOME!  For a nice test I went to a Mountain where the corners are super close and the trail is for 2 cars almost crashing. And those babys hold up to 40mph in those corners! I dont want to fall down, and mean FALL. Imagine, was like rally racing in a mountain that if you fall no 1 will rescue you, its like a 800feet drop. <P>Anyway, get AA traction temp A and 300 wear, if the tread is unidirectional is better.<P>DreX||||reg||1
Z||000018||artherd||07-11-2001||11:55 PM||||Pirelli pzero or p7000, on 17" rims if you at *all* can. so much more stability, feels as solid as a BMW, and quick as a 308 now.<P>Note: the t-top has Dunlop Supersport W10s in 215-45-17 right now, I like these a *lot* as well, nice and sticky!!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
